    "evidence": "RealityProbe packages/Integration/connectors-registry/elevate/runs/connector-elevate-1787634178034-39f0b3cc/output/elevate-read-probe.mjs (amendment round 1, 2026-08-25): the read door REJECTS a request for this field on resource ''productRegistration'' — POST fields={registration_id:true} -> HTTP 500, 59B, {\"error\":{\"message\":\"Field registration_id doesn''t exist\"}}. This is a FALSIFIED PK, not a null one: no retrievable identity column of this name exists on the read resource.",
    "resolution": "content-hash identity",
    "alternativePrimaryKeySearched": "Deliberately NOT substituted. Configuration.universalPKNote already records the corpus finding that productRegistration shows NO id-shaped field in ANY worked example anywhere (only transaction_at/pricing/dot-path selectors). payment_transaction_id is the only id-shaped documented column and is NOT an identity: it is the PAYMENT processor''s transaction id, absent on free registrations and shared across the registrations of one multi-item order. No doc-named identity column exists, and a column found only in demo response content is not eligible for Declared metadata.",
    "watermarkUnaffected": "SyncStrategy stays WatermarkIncremental — the identity demotion does not touch the fetch strategy. Both watermarks were probe-CONFIRMED as accepted filters on this resource: ''modified_at'' (HTTP 200, 29 rows in the probed window) and ''transaction_at'' (HTTP 200, 29,003 rows). ContentHashApplicable is now true as well: the watermark decides WHICH rows are fetched, the content hash decides WHICH RECORD each fetched row IS.",
    "primaryKeyReinstated": {
      "on": "2026-08-25",
      "verdict": "PARTIALLY SUPERSEDED — the READ falsification stands, the PK demotion does not.",
      "whatStands": "registration_id is NOT retrievable through the Report API `fields` allow-list (HTTP 500, \"Field registration_id doesn''t exist\"). surface=''write-only'' and excludeFromReadFieldSelector=true are unchanged, and the connector''s read selector is built from those flags alone — reinstating the PK cannot regress a read.",
      "whatWasOverCorrected": "\"Not projectable through the read door\" and \"not the record key\" are different claims. Only the first was probed. The second is affirmatively PROVEN in the other direction by ADDRESSING: the Cancellation API accepts registration_id as its sole, required record selector, and the vendor''s prose says the value identifies the order. Writing IsPrimaryKey=false asserted the unproven stronger claim and left a writable object keyless.",
      "resolutionNow": "IsPrimaryKey=true (SOFT key — no DB constraint is ever emitted) with the read-surface exclusion intact. The ''content-hash identity'' resolution recorded above is NOT withdrawn: it remains the RUNTIME mechanism by which the connector derives a stable ExternalID for read-sourced rows, and ElevateConnector.ToElevateRecord back-fills that identity into this single declared PK column so the persisted row is addressable. Field Type was widened Integer -> String so the column can hold both provenances of that identity (vendor integer on create, sha256 identity on read).",
